  "id": "indiranagar",
  "name": "Indiranagar",
  "city": "Bengaluru",
  "center": {
    "lat": 12.9719,
    "lng": 77.6412
  },
  "profile": {
    "summary": "An established east Bengaluru neighbourhood: leafy residential cross streets set back from busy shopping and dining roads, with the Purple Line metro running through it.",
    "character": "Indiranagar was laid out by the Bangalore Development Authority in the late 1970s as a suburb of bungalows and independent houses, many first owned by defence and public-sector employees. Since the IT boom of the late 1990s its main roads have turned commercial, and 100 Feet Road is now lined with shops, bars and restaurants, while pockets such as Defence Colony remain largely residential.",
    "connectivity": "Namma Metro's Purple Line has two stations in the area, Indiranagar on CMH Road and Swami Vivekananda Road. From Indiranagar, trains reach MG Road in three stops and run east towards Whitefield. BMTC buses run along CMH Road, 100 Feet Road and 80 Feet Road.",
    "goodToKnow": [
      "Late-night noise and parking from pubs on 100 Feet Road have been a long-running complaint. The Defence Colony Residents' Association was among those who took the noise to the Karnataka High Court in 2019.",
      "Footpaths are often hard to use: on 100 Feet Road two-wheelers ride and park on them at peak hours, and in Defence Colony planters and driveways push walkers onto the road (reported in September 2025).",
      "Heavy showers can waterlog Indiranagar streets quickly; a May 2026 report showed streets under water after about ten minutes of rain."
    ]
  },
